# Nginx Django Route Allowlist Sync

**Activation:** `alwaysApply: false` — when triggers in `agent-discipline-core.mdc` match, **Read this file before editing**. Triggered rules are mandatory, not optional.

Production **`proxy`** nginx answers **`/static/`**, **`/media/`**, SPA shells under **`/machine/`** and **`/pub/`**, and **`/favicon.ico`** without involving Gunicorn. Every **other** request either matches an explicit **Gunicorn allowlist** in **`services-conf/nginx-static-files.conf`** (plus generated **`nginx-api-route-allowlist.inc`** for nested **`/api/`**) or nginx returns **404** immediately.

This allowlist must stay aligned with **top-level routes intended to hit Django/DRF** through the proxy, and nested **`api/`** routes with **`EXPECTED_ROUTE_TEMPLATES`**.

## Trigger conditions (same task as the code change)

- **Add, remove, or rename** any **`path(...)`** at the **root** of **`hpcperfstats/site/hpcperfstats_site/urls.py`** (anything that defines a new first URL segment, e.g. **`/new-prefix/`**, **`new_exact`**, or **`""`** for **`/`**).
- **Add or remove** an **`include(...)`** at the root whose mount prefix is not already covered by an existing nginx **`location`** (nested **`api/`** is covered by **`nginx-api-route-allowlist.inc`**, not a blanket **`^~ /api/`**).
- **Add, remove, or rename** nested routes under **`path("api/", include(...))`** / **`api_urls.py`**: update **`EXPECTED_ROUTE_TEMPLATES`** and **regenerate** **`services-conf/nginx-api-route-allowlist.inc`** in the same task.
- **Change** **`services-conf/nginx-static-files.conf`** allowlisted **`location`** blocks, **`nginx-api-route-allowlist.inc`**, or **`services-conf/nginx-django-proxy-common.inc`** in a way that affects which URIs reach Gunicorn.

## Out of scope (no nginx allowlist update)

- **React-only** navigation: new or removed routes under **`/machine/`** or **`/pub/`** are still served by the SPA shell **`try_files`** block; they do **not** add Django HTTP endpoints unless you also add matching **`urlpatterns`** at the site root.
- **Nested API routes** are **not** covered by a blanket **`location ^~ /api/`** anymore. Unknown **`/api/...`** paths (scanner probes) hit **`location /api/ { return 404; }`** in **`nginx-static-files.conf`**.

## Required actions

1. **`services-conf/nginx-static-files.conf`**
   - For each **root** Django segment that must reach Gunicorn via **`proxy`**, add or adjust a **`location`** (exact-match **`location = ...`** for paths like **`/login_prompt`**; prefix **`location ^~ ...`** for paths like **`/oauth_callback/`**). Paths answered only from nginx static files (for example **`/robots.txt`**) must **not** use **`proxy_pass`**.
   - If you **remove** a root route from Django, remove the corresponding **`location`** (or stale probes keep forwarding useless traffic).
   - **HTTP method gate (decide for every new root route):** new proxied locations are **not** gated automatically, so whoever adds one must decide whether the view is GET-only.
     - **GET-only** (redirects, OAuth entry/callback, logout, anything that never reads `request.POST` / `request.method`): add **`if ($request_method !~ ^(GET|HEAD)$) { return 405; }`** as the first line inside the `location`, so scanner POST/PUT/OPTIONS get **405 at the edge** instead of reaching Gunicorn and logging Django CSRF failures (`Referer checking failed - no Referer`, seen from a UT watchTowr scanner, 2026-11-05). Do **not** use `limit_except GET { deny all; }`: `deny` writes an `[error] access forbidden by rule` line to the container log for every probe; a bare `return` inside `if` (the documented-safe `if` use) logs only the access line.
     - **Accepts POST** (browser CSP reports, HTML form targets such as `/test-login/`): no gate.
     - Register the location in **`_GET_ONLY_DJANGO_LOCATIONS`** or **`_POST_DJANGO_LOCATIONS`** in `test_nginx_static_wsgi_contract.py`. **`test_every_root_django_route_has_an_nginx_method_decision`** fails when a root `urlpatterns` entry is in neither list.
     - Nested **`/api/`** locations (generated allowlist) are **never** gated; DRF owns method handling there.
2. **Nested `/api/` (same task as catalog / `api_urls` changes)**
   - Update **`hpcperfstats/tests/urlconf_route_catalog.py`** **`EXPECTED_ROUTE_TEMPLATES`** (see **`pipeline-endpoint-matrix-drift-guard.mdc`**).
   - Regenerate **`services-conf/nginx-api-route-allowlist.inc`** with **`services-conf/write_nginx_api_route_allowlist_include.py`** (or fail **`test_write_nginx_api_route_allowlist_include.py`** drift).
   - Do **not** restore a blanket **`location ^~ /api/`** proxy.
3. **`hpcperfstats/site/hpcperfstats_site/tests/test_nginx_static_wsgi_contract.py`**
   - Extend or shrink **`test_nginx_static_files_conf_allowlists_django_prefixes_and_default_404`** string markers so the test continues to lock the allowlist contract whenever prefixes change (include path + catch-all **`/api/`** 404).
   - Classify the location in **`_GET_ONLY_DJANGO_LOCATIONS`** / **`_POST_DJANGO_LOCATIONS`** (method gate above).
4. **`docker-compose.defaults.yaml`**
   - If introducing a **new** included snippet path for nginx, add the matching **`proxy`** **`volumes`** mount (today **`nginx-static-files.conf`**, **`nginx-api-route-allowlist.inc`**, **`nginx-django-proxy-common.inc`**, **`nginx-compress-proxy.inc`**, **`nginx-compress-static.inc`**, **`nginx-edge-security-headers.inc`**, **`nginx-csp-no-active.inc`**, and **`nginx-csp-django-html.inc`** are mounted; SPA hash CSP includes arrive via the **`staticfiles_data`** volume). Do **not** also **`COPY`** those mount-only snippets in **`proxy.Dockerfile`**. Never place nginx config under **`/srv/static`**.

## Verification

- Run **`hpcperfstats/site/hpcperfstats_site/tests/test_nginx_static_wsgi_contract.py`** and **`hpcperfstats/tests/test_write_nginx_api_route_allowlist_include.py`** (host pytest is sufficient).
- After edits to **`nginx-static-files.conf`**, **`nginx-api-route-allowlist.inc`**, or **`nginx-django-proxy-common.inc`**, **`nginx -t`** inside the **proxy** image (or deployment nginx reload) must succeed before closing the task.

## Documentation sync

- If deployment steps or file responsibilities change, update **`HPCPerfStats/README.md`** (nginx section) and **`HPCPerfStats/docs/TESTING.md`** (nginx contract blurb) in the **same task**.

## Overlap

- **`nginx-static-url-prefix.mdc`** — **`/static/`**, SPA shell ownership, and compose volume wiring.
- **`pipeline-endpoint-matrix-drift-guard.mdc`** — canonical **`EXPECTED_ROUTE_TEMPLATES`** and pipeline HTTP matrix when routes change; **still update that catalog** for observable endpoints; this rule adds the **nginx allowlist** layer for **`proxy`** traffic only (direct **`web:8000`** hits are unaffected). Regenerating **`nginx-api-route-allowlist.inc`** is part of the same-task checklist whenever **`api/`** templates change.
